  "question": {
    "text": "A block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is in equilibrium after being suspended from the ceiling with the help of a spring of force constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>. The block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>,&nbsp;strikes the block&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;and sticks to it. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the spring&nbsp;just attains its natural length is<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/aaaa.JPG\" style=\"width: 100px; height: 195px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
